\subsection{Mass evolution and star formation efficiency}
\label{sec:massevol}

In Fig. \ref{figure:TODO} we show evolution of mass of components of our simulation.
"Aperture" corresponds to 1 pc sphere, centered at the center of the disk.
One can see that mass in the stars follows roughly a power law as $M_* \sim t^2$.
This confirms calculations of \cite{TODO:Murray}, who predicted the mass in
stars to evolve as $M_* \sim (t-t_0)^2$, where $t_0$ is time of formation of 
the first star.

Star formation efficiency after 10 kyr after the formation of the 1st sink reaches
80\% in disk only, and 50\% in the 1 pc aperture, which is high.


